API-04: return statistics in their documented units

The swmm_stat_* getters in openswmm_statistics_impl.cpp copied the internal
columns (ft, cfs, ft3, seconds) although openswmm_statistics.h documents
project length, flow and volume units and hours, so an SI project got feet
and cubic feet and every project got seconds for the "hours" statistics.
Apply to_display() to lengths, flows and volumes and divide times by 3600,
in the scalar and bulk getters. swmm_node_get_stat_time_flooded() and
swmm_link_get_stat_surcharge_time(), documented in hours, also returned
seconds.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-04_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/openswmm_links_impl.cpp b/src/engine/core/openswmm_links_impl.cpp
index 9963ab2..0e439c4 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/openswmm_links_impl.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/openswmm_links_impl.cpp
@@ -1678,7 +1678,7 @@ SWMM_ENGINE_API int swmm_link_get_stat_surcharge_time(SWMM_Engine engine, int id
     CHECK_HANDLE(engine);
     const auto& ctx = to_engine(engine)->context();
     CHECK_INDEX(idx >= 0 && idx < ctx.n_links());
-    if (val) *val = ctx.links.stat_time_surcharged[static_cast<std::size_t>(idx)];
+    if (val) *val = ctx.links.stat_time_surcharged[static_cast<std::size_t>(idx)] / 3600.0; // sec -> hours
     return SWMM_OK;
 }
 
